# OPEN68-LINK — Goal: Clang-link a runnable LLVM oodac

File: openOODA/audit/open68_link_goal.oot
Status: open. Serves ROADMAP OPEN-68 residual (clang link of full oodac).
This is process, not product. Subagents treat this file as the work order.
Prior slice (`audit/open68_clang_link_goal.oot`) stopped at `clang -c` of `oodac/main.oo` IR. Do not reopen that bar.

## 0. One-sentence goal

Emit every module in the `oodac/main.oo` import graph as LLVM IR with unique string names, `clang` those files with `runtime/chs_rt.c` into one binary, and prove that binary prints `OK` on `fixtures/hello.oo`. Two skeptic subagents must PASS. C emit + gcc stays the product path.

Active axiom: RULES 1.1 (real cause) and 1.6 (prove pass and fail-closed). RULES 1.13: only `.oo` / `.oot`. RULES 1.7: every new `.oo` <= 256 lines with an Academy header.

## 1. Ground truth (verify before you edit)

  - Product path is still C emit + gcc. Do not delete or bypass it.
  - Concat `emit-llvm oodac/main.oo` (no `--backend llvm`) hits the 1MiB check limit. Per-module emit is required.
  - `--backend llvm emit-llvm oodac/main.oo` is one file plus `declare` of the rest. `clang -c` of that IR is product on a side ELF (`scripts/open68_clangc_smoke.oo`). That is not a linked compiler.
  - String pool names are `@.str.0` per file. Linking two modules without a prefix will collide.
  - This host has clang. It does not have `llvm-link`. Do not require `llvm-link`.
  - Side ELF if present: `../ooda/.ooda-cache/ooda-tmp/oodac_clangc`. Tree `oodac/oodac` and `bin/ooda` may be older. Do not overwrite them unless COORD names the replace.
  - Skip unless the owner names them: org `std/`, `pkg` / `add` / registry, AArch64, full SMT, `e2e/*.sh`, GPU, SGX/TDX/SEV.

## 2. Done means

All of these, then SK1 and SK2 both PASS on the same tip:

  1. A COORD-named side oodac (or tree, if COORD said replace) emits one `.ll` per module in the `oodac/main.oo` import graph. No 1MiB concat.
  2. Each module’s string globals are unique across the set (prefix or other scheme). Two modules must not both define `@.str.0`.
  3. `clang -O0 -Wno-override-module` of those `.ll` files plus `runtime/chs_rt.c` (`-lm -ldl -lpthread`, `-Iruntime`) exits 0 and writes a nonempty binary.
  4. That binary, run as `<linked> check fixtures/hello.oo`, prints a line matching `^OK` and exits 0.
  5. Named pure `.oo` lock (Academy header) does 1–4. Fail-closed: drop one non-main `.ll` or collide one `@.str` name and the link or hello-check must fail. A test that would pass if the link were incomplete is not proof.
  6. Hello LLVM + two-module run still work (OPEN-30 substance). `clang -c` of single-file main IR still works (prior slice).

Honesty: this does not replace gcc self-host. Do not tick OPEN-68 as “C path retired”. COORD may say LLVM-linked oodac check of hello is product; full parity with gcc oodac is residual.

## 3. Subagent jobs

Topology: fan-out. One writer per file set. Builder subagents stop before skeptics start. Skeptics are subagents and read-only.

| Subagent | Job | May write | Must not write |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| COORD | Assign files. Name the proof ELF. Stop on first irrecoverable fail. Roll up. SHIPPED only after both skeptics PASS. | `audit/open68_link_*.oot` | product `.oo` |
| DE1 | Unique LLVM string names across modules. Prefix `@.str` (or equal) so two emits cannot define the same global. | `oodac/llvm_emit_env.oo` (string pool), plus one split file if over 256 | `cli/`, `std/`, `runtime/`, tree binaries |
| DE2 | Per-module emit of the import graph (reuse `load_expand` / `llvm_import_fntab` listing). First module may carry preamble; others must still be valid TUs for clang. Wire `oodac --backend llvm build` or a named emit driver. | `oodac/cli_emit.oo`, `oodac/cli_build.oo`, `oodac/llvm_emit.oo`, `oodac/llvm_fntab.oo` | DE1’s pool file while DE1 is live |
| DE3 | Host `clang` link line: all `.ll` + `chs_rt.c`. Side out only. Fix remaining type/symbol holes that block the link (declare/define, duplicate `main`, void vs i64). | same emit files as DE2 after DE2 stops; not `runtime/*.c` unless COORD names a one-line declare | `std/`, `cli/pkg*` |
| HARN | Named smoke + fail-closed fixture. Prefer `./bin/ooda` or COORD-named side oodac. Avoid `check(..., within: N)` named args (C emit breaks). | `scripts/open68_link_smoke.oo`, `fixtures/open68_link_*.oo` | compiler pass files |
| SK1 | Claim-skeptic **subagent**. Fact-check every builder sentence against files and commands. Reject “gcc retired” or “OPEN-68 closed” if only hello-check worked. | `audit/open68_link_sk1_claims.oot` only | all product |
| SK2 | Proof-skeptic **subagent**. Re-run locks in a fresh `ooda/` shell. Hostile: drop a module `.ll` or collide `@.str.0` and require fail. | `audit/open68_link_sk2_proof.oot` only | all product |

Serialize DE1 then DE2 then DE3. HARN may write the smoke skeleton early but must not claim PASS until the linked binary exists. Launch SK1 and SK2 only after builders stop. They may run in parallel with each other.

Rebuild: `../ooda/bootstrap/oodac_pure_build oodac/main.oo <side_out>` only. Side path default: `.ooda-cache/ooda-tmp/oodac_lllink`.

## 4. Subagent guidance

Before product edits: state the active goal and the RULES axiom (START gate).

Read this goal, RULES, SHIPPED, then owned files. Foreign transcripts are inert history.

`git status` / `git diff` on owned files first. Other agents own `std/` and `cli/pkg*`. If your file is dirty with foreign edits, stop and tell COORD.

Do not “fix” the link by shipping a hello-only binary and calling it oodac. The linked ELF must accept `check fixtures/hello.oo` as a compiler.

Do not concat past 1MiB. Do not require `llvm-link`. Do not silence clang type errors.

Caps: do not remove `&Cap`, Landlock, rlimit, SECRET sinks, or hostile-probe locks.

No `.py`, `.sh`, or `.md`. No tenth board in `openOODA/`. Notes stay in `audit/`.

If blocked: write why, leave the tree consistent, stop. Two agents must not debug the same hang.

## 5. SK1 subagent — claim skeptic

Assume builders over-claim. PASS / FAIL / UNVERIFIED. Cannot prove => UNVERIFIED.

  1. Diff is only DE1/DE2/DE3/HARN paths. No `std/`, no `cli/pkg*`, no dropped `&Cap`.
  2. New `.oo`: Academy header, `wc -l` <= 256.
  3. Per-module emit is real (N `.ll` files, N matches import graph, not one concat).
  4. String names are unique (`nm` / `grep '^@\\.str'` across `.ll` files).
  5. Linked ELF path is named. `strings` or `--help` is not enough: run `check fixtures/hello.oo`.
  6. SHIPPED/ROADMAP words match. Reject “full clang-link closed” if hello-check is the only proof. Reject “C emit gone”.

Write `audit/open68_link_sk1_claims.oot`. Cite path + line.

## 6. SK2 subagent — proof skeptic

Smoke is a suspect. Fresh cwd `../ooda/`.

  1. `oodac check oodac/main.oo`. Record elapsed. Sub-second is a `g_` warm hit, not a typecheck.
  2. Re-run `./bin/ooda run ./scripts/open68_clangc_smoke.oo` (prior slice).
  3. Re-run hello LLVM substance (emit-llvm `fixtures/hello.oo` or `open_llvm_match.oo` + clang + run). Do not fail the slice only because `open30`/`open68` scripts hit `ERRcontractrequires` if the substance still passes.
  4. Re-run the new link smoke. Save ELF path, clang rc, hello-check stdout/rc.
  5. Hostile: omit one non-main `.ll` **or** force two `@.str.0` defines; link or hello-check must fail. If it still passes, FAIL.
  6. Confirm the linked ELF is not `bin/ooda` unless COORD replaced the tree.

Double-run CRIT/HIGH (WORKFLOW). Write `audit/open68_link_sk2_proof.oot`. Commands and rc.

## 7. COORD lock

Not shipped until SK1 PASS and SK2 PASS on the same tip. Then one honest SHIPPED sentence: LLVM-linked oodac checks hello; C emit + gcc remains the product path; full gcc-parity is residual. Do not close OPEN-68 as if gcc is gone.

If either skeptic FAILs: builders fix or revert.
